    ## The release binaries the run log uses
    
    `specs/0027-read-back.md`, "P3", has the part's two samples run again
    with the binaries this log hashed. `emend-copy` and `xlsx-diff` are
    built in the release profile for the host and for i686-unknown-linux-musl in
    `records/logs/m3p5-p3/size.log`, each printed there on a line
    `hash: <name> <target> <sha256>`, and the run log compares the sha256 of
    what it runs with the one this log printed, reading it out of this log by
    command.
    
    ## Reading these figures
    
    File sizes on this target change in whole 4096-byte steps. They are not
    themselves whole pages: all the probes leave the same remainder, 2596
    bytes, modulo 4096, so it is every DIFFERENCE between them that is a whole
    number of pages. A change under a page is therefore invisible in the file
    size, while the section totals, from `size -A`, resolve to the byte. Both
    are given for every figure above.
